From 1427e306cd42a187257f7f4ca806d53d4584b69f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:05:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 198/209] fix(area): unique GUID hiparts for the gravity volume
 and the distributor

Adding either component to an entity made the WHOLE entity's inspector go
blank - the shape's panel included, whatever kind the shape was, in either
order. The cause is not in the reflected data at all.

CEntityObject::CreateComponentWidgets keys each component's property tree by

    GetClassDesc().GetGUID().hipart + componentTypeIndex   (EntityObject.cpp:1107)

i.e. by the FIRST HALF of the component GUID only. CInspectorWidgetCreator then
treats a duplicate id as a widget that several selected objects share: it skips
the second registration and bumps usageCount (InspectorWidgetCreator.h:72-78),
and at the end of the scope it erases every widget whose usageCount does not
equal the number of objects in the scope (:40-43). With one entity selected the
count is 1, the collided entry has 2, and BOTH panels are erased - which is
exactly what "every component disappears" looks like.

All six components of this module were minted from one series,
6C3A81D5-0F47-4E9A-B4D1-72E5C8A962xx, differing only in the LOPART. For the four
shape kinds that is harmless, because they declare each other incompatible and
two of them can never sit on one entity. A function component sits BESIDE a
shape, and the distributor sits beside the gravity volume, so those three needed
three different hiparts. The two new ones are now

    Gravity Volume  {9A31F4C7-5E28-4B60-8D19-2C7B6E05A340}
    Distributor     {4F82D6B1-7C93-4A15-B2E6-58D0913FC7A2}

and both ReflectType()s carry the rule as a comment so the next component does
not inherit the trap. The shape GUIDs are deliberately NOT changed: they are
already in saved levels, and their shared hipart cannot bite.

Consequence: a gravity volume or distributor saved by the previous build is
addressed by its old GUID and will not be found again. There were only test
entities, so they are re-added rather than migrated.

The second reported symptom - a brush-flag row whose label intermittently turned
into garbage - has no separate cause in this module: every SetLabel,
SetDescription, AddMember szName/szLabel/szDescription, AddConstant and
Serialize label in the three files is a string literal, every szName matches
[A-Za-z0-9_]+, and AddMember copies its default value into a CDefaultValue
rather than keeping a pointer to the temporary (TypeDesc.h:592). The most likely
explanation is the collision above: a property tree that was registered and then
erased leaves rows whose labels no longer belong to it. To be retested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../Module/Functions/DistributorComponent.h              | 5 ++++-
 .../Module/Functions/GravityVolumeComponent.h            | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/DistributorComponent.h b/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/DistributorComponent.h
index 06232093..9751f2d0 100644
--- a/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/DistributorComponent.h
+++ b/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/DistributorComponent.h
@@ -165,7 +165,10 @@ public:
 
 	static void ReflectType(Schematyc::CTypeDesc<CDistributorComponent>& desc)
 	{
-		desc.SetGUID("{6C3A81D5-0F47-4E9A-B4D1-72E5C8A96211}"_cry_guid);
+		// Its own hipart, distinct from every shape kind's AND from the gravity volume's - see the
+		// comment on CGravityVolumeComponent::ReflectType. A distributor and a gravity volume can
+		// share one entity, so sharing a hipart would blank that entity's inspector.
+		desc.SetGUID("{4F82D6B1-7C93-4A15-B2E6-58D0913FC7A2}"_cry_guid);
 		desc.SetEditorCategory("Area");
 		desc.SetLabel("Distributor");
 		desc.SetDescription("Places meshes along the spline shape on this entity.");
diff --git a/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/GravityVolumeComponent.h b/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/GravityVolumeComponent.h
index 7271f1dc..ec0c6d88 100644
--- a/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/GravityVolumeComponent.h
+++ b/Code/CryPlugins/AreaComponents/Module/Functions/GravityVolumeComponent.h
@@ -44,7 +44,14 @@ public:
 
 	static void ReflectType(Schematyc::CTypeDesc<CGravityVolumeComponent>& desc)
 	{
-		desc.SetGUID("{6C3A81D5-0F47-4E9A-B4D1-72E5C8A96210}"_cry_guid);
+		// The HIPART of a component's GUID has to be unique among the components that can sit on
+		// ONE entity. CEntityObject::CreateComponentWidgets keys each component's property tree by
+		// GetClassDesc().GetGUID().hipart + instanceIndex (EntityObject.cpp:1107), so two different
+		// component classes whose GUIDs differ only in the LOPART collide on that key and the whole
+		// entity's inspector goes blank. The shape kinds may all share the 6C3A81D5-0F47-4E9A
+		// hipart because they are mutually incompatible - never two on one entity - but a function
+		// component sits BESIDE a shape and beside the other functions, so it needs its own.
+		desc.SetGUID("{9A31F4C7-5E28-4B60-8D19-2C7B6E05A340}"_cry_guid);
 		desc.SetEditorCategory("Area");
 		desc.SetLabel("Gravity Volume");
 		desc.SetDescription("Turns the spline shape on this entity into a tube of physics gravity.");
